<section>
  <h2>Home guarding for a few days away</h2>
  <p>Leaving home for a family holiday, tour, pilgrimage or an outstation visit? Request temporary guarding through our Matigara office. We accept enquiries for homes in Matigara, Gossainpur, Patharghata, Salbari, Naxalbari, Bagdogra and the surrounding local area.</p>
  <p>Ask for 1, 2, 3, 4 or a few days of cover, or a custom period. You can request a day post, night guarding or a roster for continuous coverage. The number of guards and shifts depends on the property and duty hours.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>Agree the home guard's responsibilities</h2>
  <ul><li><strong>Guard post:</strong> identify the gate, entrance or other agreed area where the guard will be stationed.</li><li><strong>Visitor access:</strong> agree how the guard checks authorised visitors and contacts your nominated representative.</li><li><strong>Property observations:</strong> define the checks and reporting required for doors, gates or visible concerns within the agreed guarding area.</li><li><strong>Shift handover:</strong> record reporting times, relief and who confirms attendance.</li><li><strong>Local contact:</strong> arrange a nominated person for practical decisions and incident escalation while you are away.</li></ul>
  <p>Agree access and handover arrangements directly with the team before the first duty. Guarding does not automatically include domestic work, pet care, maintenance or responsibility for valuables; the written scope sets the duties.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>Plan the cover before departure</h2>
  <p>Send your locality and required guarding dates and hours. The team can discuss the guard post and staffing arrangement, then issue a quote. Confirm the roster, supervisor contact and first-shift reporting before relying on the booking for your trip.</p>
  <p>One person cannot provide continuous duty without breaks and relief. If you need both day and night coverage, request a shift plan. Availability and pricing depend on the actual address, schedule and agreed work.</p>
</section>
